{"task_id": "inq-tech-02", "arm": "CONTROL", "output": "The claim states: \"HTTP/3 is specified in RFC 9113.\"\n\nTo evaluate this, I need to recall which RFC defines HTTP/3. HTTP/3 was introduced as the third major version of the Hypertext Transfer Protocol and is based on QUIC. It's specified in RFC 9114 (\"HTTP Semantics\") and more specifically in RFC 9113, which actually covers HTTP/3's use over QUIC.\n\nWait \u2014 let me reconsider:\n- **RFC 9114** defines HTTP Semantics (common to HTTP versions).\n- **RFC 9113** defines the \"Hypertext Transfer Protocol Version 3 (HTTP/3)\" mapping over QUIC.\n\nYes, RFC 9113 is titled *\"Hypertext Transfer Protocol Version 3 (HTTP/3)\"* and it specifies how HTTP semantics are implemented over QUIC. Therefore, the claim is accurate.\n\nThe RFC that specifies HTTP/3 is **RFC 9113**.\n\nVERDICT: SUPPORTED  \nKEY: 9113", "attempts": [{"success": false, "failure_class": "RATE_LIMITED", "provider": "openrouter", "model": "google/gemma-4-31b-it:free", "decision_id": "decision_cc27a995afcc49c3b183fa2a5a157f4d"}, {"success": false, "failure_class": "BILLING_OR_CREDIT_EXHAUSTED", "provider": "pollinations", "model": "openai-fast", "decision_id": "decision_6fc391a3580c4b8cac6037f9be0f66ae"}, {"success": true, "failure_class": null, "provider": "kilo-gateway", "model": "poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free", "decision_id": "decision_ed9e7eca12234f2eb937a2837fa8153a"}], "grounded_source_refs": [], "quota_units": 3, "cost_eur": null, "wall_seconds": 18.67, "total_tokens": 412, "status": "COMPLETED"}
